## Processes
- [Document Numbering & Filing — Fishbone Group policy](Process-Document-Numbering-and-Filing.md) — the one group-wide, **locked, versioned** instruction set for registering, numbering (per-entity prefixes, 7-digit) and filing documents; defines the single Document Register, project-co-located filing in Collaboration Space, dedup-on-entry, the inter-KB `Raw/` document hand-off (§7a), tasks-are-not-documents (§6), per-KB self-migration of the back-catalogue (§11), self-assigned 4-digit property codes and property-folder filing (§3/§7), email-attachment source capture (§5), and the change-requests feedback loop. (v1.3, Active)
- [Incoming Post (paper mail) handling — Fishbone Group process](Process-Post-Handling.md) — the group "post room" procedure for physical mail received at the shared office for all seven companies: open → scan → single group `Raw/Paper Mail/` intake → triage (owning company from the letter) → register in the group Document Register (Direction = Incoming) and file in Collaboration Space → route to the owning company's KB `/Raw` via §7a (Waste / group-level kept by the group). Feeds the numbering policy; adds no new numbering. (v1.1, Active)
- [Housekeeping & Session Discipline — Fishbone Group process](Process-Housekeeping-and-Session-Discipline.md) — the group standard for keeping every Fishbone knowledge system documented, current and tidy: a single Definition of Done and copy-paste templates (control files, dated change-log entries, archive-then-recreate, no stray root duplicates). Owner-authorised 2026-09-14; **Alex** (the Housekeeping & Operations Steward) is the named owner and enforces it via the weekly Housekeeping sweep. (v1, Active)
- [Request-Pool Intake — Fishbone Group standard](Process-Request-Pool-Intake.md) — how every routine picks up ad-hoc work assigned to it on the AI Workforce Hub "Tasks & Requests" pool (`8860839228606340`) before its own beat: read own `Open`/`In Progress` rows oldest-first, do up to 3 within charter + own connectors, write `Response / result` + `Status`/`Done date`, flag anything outside authority for a human. Grants no new authority (own-row Hub writes are the one boundary clarification; Peter takes a narrow carve-out). Promoted from Alex's AWT-0011 standard; the full-replacement routine prompts live in the group KB `Routine-Changes/`. (v1, Active)
- [Company / Officer Due-Diligence Footprint — Fishbone Group process](Process-Due-Diligence-Officer-Footprint.md) — the reusable, confidence-tiered method + template for a Companies House footprint report on any UK company or officer (customer, client, counterparty, or the group's own directors), from public register data only. Pairs the fillable `Outputs/Template_Company-Officer-Due-Diligence-Report.html` with the data recipe (officer search → per-officer appointments → per-company profile/PSC/charges/filing-history) and a strict public-data boundary. Worked example: the "Director Footprint" report v3. (v1, Active)

